name: Source drift retains partial coverage and decisions until an explicit stable scan
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | baseline-prerequisite
keys: a
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART baseline
require-live-snap: 35 1 finding(s) | baseline-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned source settlement marker | baseline-observation
submit: decision deferred Owned static marker needs operator review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | deferred-observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
ask: Does one actual local rule observation retain a clearly scripted human deferral without claiming vulnerability validity or executing target source?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare-drift
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | drift-prerequisite
keys: a
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART release-with-edit
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
require-live-snap: 35 Source could not be verified | partial-source-receipt
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-after-drift
expect-not: not observed in a later covered run
resize: 160x48
live-snap: retained-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: retained-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: retained-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: retained-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 F-0001 · FINDING | finding-reader
resize: 40x12
live-snap: retained-40x12
expect: F-0001
expect: PgUp/PgDn read
ask: Does Review preserve the earlier signal and decision after partial work, with the selected identity and reading controls usable at six sizes?
resize: 120x36
keys: q
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Displayed Scan: partial | partial-history-report
expect: Scope: workspace history
expect: Scan receipt does not establish complete repository coverage.
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial-report
ask: Does the report describe recorded history without claiming complete current-source coverage after the source mismatch?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART stable
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | stable-prerequisite
keys: a
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART complete
require-live-snap: 35 0 finding(s) | stable-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-after-complete
expect: not observed
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Does only the explicitly requested stable scan establish covered absence while the earlier deferral and partial run remain in history?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | recovered-review
expect: not observed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scan_source_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain all three local scans, partial coverage and one human decision with zero provider requests or target execution?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
